ub.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5145925527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5145925527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMriXlw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-31T17:54:29Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T17:54:29Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5145925527/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5307649872","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5307649872","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5307649872,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPFxPUA","user":{"login":"Spacexcx","id":175117217,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnAToQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175117217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx","html_url":"https://github.com/Spacexcx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T13:23:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T13:23:13Z","body":"Hey — came across this PR while testing an approach for predicting which parts of a diff need closer reviewer attention (based on analyzing merged PRs + review history). For this one, before checking the actual review thread, the analysis flagged the exact same gap bruvzg caught — that set_use_own_world_3d had the same unchecked find_world_3d() call as set_world_3d. Matched the real review outcome pretty closely here.\r\n\r\nCurious whether something like this (automatic, per-PR, flagging what's likely to need a second look) would actually be useful in your workflow, or if it's solving a problem that isn't really there day-to-day.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5307649872/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5308738768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5308738768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5308738768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPGzs0A","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T17:35:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T17:35:11Z","body":"@Spacexcx I had the same finding when an AI reviewed my work locally before opening this PR (did not use it to write the code). I dismissed it to keep the fix narrow, and only expanded it at the suggestion of a human.\r\n\r\nAutomatic AI flagging on GitHub pull requests is undesired and is generally considered spam. Any AI tools used on Godot need to be done outside GitHub, in a limited capacity, in a way that is completely filtered by humans so that everything that reaches the eyes of PR reviewers has a complete authorship and full understanding from the human PR author. So to be clear, I personally find AI tools to have value, but that value does not take the form of anything on GitHub, nor does it take the form of writing significant amounts of new content.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5308738768/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5310513444","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5310513444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5310513444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPIgBJA","user":{"login":"Spacexcx","id":175117217,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnAToQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175117217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx","html_url":"https://github.com/Spacexcx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T00:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T00:31:18Z","body":"@aaronfranke That's really helpful context, thanks — makes sense, and matches what I'd guess about how most maintainers feel about anything automated showing up on GitHub itself.\r\n\r\nSounds like the useful form of this is closer to what you already do: something local/CLI-based that runs before you open the PR, fully under your control, not visible to anyone unless you choose to act on it. If a tool like that existed — flagging likely-risky files/lines before you push, with the kind of grounded reasoning we saw match your own review here — is that something you'd actually reach for, or does your current local AI review already cover that gap well enough?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5310513444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5310853212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5310853212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5310853212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPI0wXA","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T01:42:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T01:43:32Z","body":"@Spacexcx That's the kind of tool I am most interested in. Existing general-purpose AI tools already cover this, but there is probably an opportunity to do better, or at least make it easier. The critical kill condition being that such a tool must not require interaction with GitHub, so as to keep \"AI slop\" from wasting the time of maintainers. The same probably also applies to most other open source projects.\r\n\r\nI should mention, this GitHub repo is for development of Godot Engine, so this is fairly off-topic. Also, you are a brand new account, so I have no idea if you're even a real person or an AI spam bot yourself. I'm writing this message anyway just in case someone stumbles across your question and wants an answer.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5310853212/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5322475565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5322475565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5322475565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPT6ILQ","user":{"login":"Spacexcx","id":175117217,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnAToQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175117217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx","html_url":"https://github.com/Spacexcx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T01:56:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T01:56:51Z","body":"@aaronfranke Went ahead and built a rough version of what we talked about — a local CLI script, no GitHub interaction at all. It reads your git diff, sends it to an LLM with a prompt tuned from analyzing ~15 real merged PRs (including this one), and prints flagged files with a required exact-quote from the diff as evidence (to cut down on speculative flags). Runs entirely on your machine, nothing posted anywhere.\r\n\r\nStill rough — it catches things like unchecked null derefs and config/wiring risk well, but I just found it misses logic-vs-intent mismatches (e.g. a condition that contradicts its own docstring) unless I explicitly prompt for that category. Working on tightening that up.\r\n\r\nNo pressure at all, but if you'd ever be willing to point it at a real diff of yours (or just tell me it's not worth pursuing further), I'd genuinely value the input — you've already saved me from building the wrong thing once.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5322475565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5458925834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121940#issuecomment-5458925834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121940","id":5458925834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRWCZCg","user":{"login":"Spacexcx","id":175117217,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnAToQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175117217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx","html_url":"https://github.com/Spacexcx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spacexcx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T23:46:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T23:46:38Z","body":"Hey — following up on our conversation on \r\n#121940. Packaged the tool into a proper repo with a README: github.com/Spacexcx/pr-check\r\n\r\nRan it against a small batch of merged Godot PRs since we talked — caught a real concurrency issue, correctly stayed quiet on clean ones, and (this is the part I want to be upfront about) produced one confident-but-wrong flag on a mutex/deadlock claim. Added a second pass that catches exactly that kind of error now.\r\n\r\nNo pressure — but if you ever want to point it at one of your own diffs, genuinely curious how it holds up outside my own testing.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5458925834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]